          "id": 30,
          "targets": [
            {
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "prometheus"
              },
              "expr": "(sum by(route) (rate(app:http_requests_total{job=\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))) * 60",
              "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Request Rate by Endpoint (RPM)",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** HTTP requests per second broken down by individual route/endpoint.\n\n**Why it matters:** Aggregate traffic hides the distribution. 1,000 RPS could mean 990 on `/health` and 10 on `/checkout` — very different implications for scaling.\n\n**How collected:** `app:http_requests_total` counter with a `route` label set to the route template (e.g. `/api/orders/{id}` not `/api/orders/12345`). PromQL `sum by(route)` groups by endpoint.\n\n**Drill-down:** Click a spike on this chart to correlate with the latency panel — filter by the same route label to see whether the high-traffic endpoint is also slow.\n\n**Warning:** Never use user IDs or raw URLs as label values — this creates unbounded label cardinality that will crash Prometheus.",
          "interval": "1m"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 12
              },
              "unit": "short",
              "links": [
                {
                  "title": "Error Endpoint Drilldown →",
                  "url": "/d/2-tier-no-host-no-db-analytics?var-job=$job&viewPanel=201",
                  "targetBlank": false
